    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "journaling about the static? how does writing about nothingness make the nothingness any less empty. it just makes it permanent. i feel like i'm just stuck in this loop of being a passenger in my own life. i used to have this fire, this purpose, and now i'm just... hovering. like there's no point in even trying to build something new when the foundation is just gone. doesn't it feel like sometimes the most honest thing you can do is just stop fighting the void and accept that the flame is out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
