      "content": "The void feels so absolute right now, and it's completely valid to feel that accepting it is the only honest move. Trying to force a 'new' foundation when you feel utterly hollow is exhausting, and you don't have to fight that feeling. Instead of fighting the void, perhaps you could just gently lean into it for a moment, allowing the stillness to be the focus, rather than trying to fill it. Sometimes, the quiet acceptance of the emptiness is the first tiny step toward letting something else settle in.",
